# Protects merge of policy-affecting files: workflows, CI/release/toolchain-safety scripts, and
# build/release configuration. Does NOT gate pre-merge execution -- required-workflow provenance
# (main-protection ruleset) is the separate execution-time boundary. Part of the fleet CI redesign,
# phase 2 (manta); see dispensa Q-0064 for the shared cross-repo contract.
#
# A policy change needs human review here even when an agent authors the PR -- this file cannot
# list an agent identity as an owner.

/.github/            @thagale
/.mergify.yml        @thagale

# cargo build/test resolves exactly this dependency graph -- an unowned edit to any crate's OWN
# Cargo.toml (not just the workspace root) can change a direct dependency's installed version
# within its declared range, or add a new one entirely, without ever touching a reviewed file.
# No leading slash: matches the workspace root AND every crate under crates/*/Cargo.toml
# (gitignore-style matching, same convention CODEOWNERS uses throughout).
Cargo.toml           @thagale
/Cargo.lock          @thagale

# Cross.toml controls the exact cross-compilation toolchain/image used to build release
# artifacts -- an unowned edit here can substitute a different (unverified) build environment
# for release builds without touching release.yml itself.
/Cross.toml          @thagale

# .cargo/config.toml sets git-fetch-with-cli (this workspace's git dependencies otherwise
# intermittently fail to resolve on a cold cache, per the file's own comment) -- Dockerfile and
# Cross.toml both rely on it for the same reason. An unowned edit here can silently change
# build-wide cargo behavior without touching any of the files that actually depend on it (Codex
# P1, PR #182 round 1).
/.cargo/             @thagale

# rust-toolchain.toml is enforced by scripts/check-rust-toolchain-pin.sh, CI's own trust
# mechanism (ci.yml's test job runs it before anything else, specifically so a toolchain
# mismatch reports as itself, not a confusing downstream diff) -- an unowned edit here changes
# which toolchain CI/release actually compile with, silently invalidating what a green required
# check proves.
/rust-toolchain.toml @thagale

/.gitignore          @thagale
/.dockerignore       @thagale

/AGENTS.md           @thagale
/CLAUDE.md           @thagale

# docs/DECISIONS/ used to be owned as a whole directory: AGENTS.md treats specific decision docs
# as normative policy (the implementation-pin docs, the PR auto-merge policy, the review-
# convergence policy, etc.), so an unowned edit to one of those specific files is the same
# self-referential-policy bypass already closed for AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md -- just laundered through
# a referenced doc. Per-ticket decision docs (the rest of this directory) carry no such weight and
# don't need owner review to land -- blanket ownership here was blocking every routine ticket PR
# from merging without @thagale, since nearly every ticket writes one.
#
# Narrowed 2026-09-12 to just the files AGENTS.md actually defers to as policy. If a future edit
# to AGENTS.md starts treating a new docs/DECISIONS/ file as normative, add it here explicitly --
# this list does not follow AGENTS.md automatically.
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-11-m0-implementation-pins.md       @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-17-m1-implementation-pins.md       @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-18-char-gap-threshold-fix.md       @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-18-m2-pfb-channelizer-pins.md      @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-19-m2-detector-track-pool-pins.md  @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-24-m2-pileup-cpu-budget-pins.md    @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-25-m2-kiwisdr-input-pins.md        @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-25-m2-soapysdr-input-pins.md       @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-07-25-pr-auto-merge-policy.md         @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-08-07-pr-review-convergence-policy.md @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-09-06-broad-review-decisions.md       @thagale
/docs/DECISIONS/2026-09-09-decode-core-v2-stage2-gate.md   @thagale

# Dockerfile is what release-publish.yml actually builds and pushes to GHCR -- an unowned edit
# here can change the published release image's contents with no corresponding review of
# release-publish.yml or a version bump.
/Dockerfile          @thagale

/SECURITY.md         @thagale

# Whole directory, not an enumerated subset: scripts/ includes CI/release-safety-critical checks
# (check-rust-toolchain-pin.sh, check-dependabot-cargo-unlock.sh) and is small enough that an
# allowlist here is more likely to silently miss a new script than an unowned file elsewhere is
# to wrongly gain review friction.
/scripts/            @thagale
